1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,783
The Great Wall. Visible from space.

2
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:05,983
Except... it isn't.

3
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:08,183
The Great Wall myth.

4
00:00:08,333 --> 00:00:11,717
The wall is long. Thousands of miles.

5
00:00:11,867 --> 00:00:14,383
But it's only a few metres wide.

6
00:00:14,533 --> 00:00:18,483
From orbit, that's like spotting a hair from miles away.

7
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:22,450
It's also the same colour as the ground.

8
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,783
In 2003, China's first astronaut looked.

9
00:00:26,933 --> 00:00:28,983
He couldn't see it.

10
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:31,683
So where did the myth come from?

11
00:00:31,833 --> 00:00:35,450
People claimed it before anyone went to space.

12
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:40,250
A 1932 cartoon said you could see it from the Moon.

13
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:43,983
From the Moon, you can barely make out continents.

14
00:00:44,133 --> 00:00:47,150
School books repeated it for decades.

15
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:50,650
What can you see from orbit? Cities at night.

16
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,083
With a zoom lens? Maybe the wall too.

17
00:00:54,233 --> 00:00:56,350
But not with your eyes.

18
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:58,850
Still an amazing wall.

19
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,117
Walls visible from the Moon: zero.

20
00:01:02,267 --> 00:01:05,550
Anyway, here's the wall from space.
